1
00:00:00,830 --> 00:00:04,010
Yaga, what is that thing?

2
00:00:04,480 --> 00:00:06,760
It is possible to have
man-made cursed corpses

3
00:00:06,760 --> 00:00:10,840
act more autonomously than
other forms of manipulation.

4
00:00:10,840 --> 00:00:13,080
But they're always powered by

5
00:00:13,080 --> 00:00:15,860
consuming cursed energy
from the sorcerer.

6
00:00:15,860 --> 00:00:20,370
Yet that thing is sustaining
itself on its own cursed energy.

7
00:00:22,230 --> 00:00:25,570
The higher-ups are currently trying
to designate you as a special-grade

8
00:00:25,570 --> 00:00:28,960
and officially sentence you
to indefinite imprisonment.

9
00:00:29,780 --> 00:00:33,810
Because if you can intentionally
create that thing,

10
00:00:33,810 --> 00:00:37,310
you could easily have your own army.

11
00:00:38,010 --> 00:00:40,260
Answer me, Yaga.

12
00:00:41,430 --> 00:00:47,020
Do you truly not know how
that thing was made?

13
00:00:49,750 --> 00:00:50,630
Correct.

14
00:00:51,820 --> 00:00:53,370
Masamichi.

15
00:00:54,410 --> 00:00:56,380
Everyone's worried about you.

16
00:00:56,380 --> 00:00:57,950
They say you seem down.

17
00:00:58,200 --> 00:00:59,630
I see.

18
00:01:01,950 --> 00:01:03,920
So I told them all this!

19
00:01:03,920 --> 00:01:06,910
If you're feeling down,
we just have to cheer you up!

20
00:01:09,300 --> 00:01:10,570
That so?

21
00:01:11,250 --> 00:01:12,730
I'm a genius, aren't I?

22
00:01:13,250 --> 00:01:14,700
Yeah.

23
00:01:15,670 --> 00:01:19,550
Takeru, I'm sorry, but I won't be
able to come home for a while.

24
00:01:19,960 --> 00:01:22,270
Please let the others know, too.

25
00:01:22,270 --> 00:01:24,080
Leaving for work again?

26
00:01:24,080 --> 00:01:26,960
Yeah. It'll be a long trip.

27
00:01:26,960 --> 00:01:28,190
Don't worry.

28
00:01:28,190 --> 00:01:31,540
This forest is protected by Tengen-sama.

29
00:01:31,540 --> 00:01:35,200
Your mother will come see you again, too.

30
00:01:36,620 --> 00:01:39,690
You'll be all right without me.

31
00:01:43,090 --> 00:01:44,490
Masamichi.

32
00:01:45,160 --> 00:01:47,870
It'll be lonely without you, Masamichi.

33
00:01:52,910 --> 00:01:55,250
Are you sure, Kusakabe?

34
00:01:55,250 --> 00:01:58,380
Don't go telling anyone I helped you.

35
00:01:58,380 --> 00:02:01,760
You were captured to lure Yaga-san out.

36
00:02:02,760 --> 00:02:05,510
And I owe that man a favor.

37
00:02:06,550 --> 00:02:08,370
Go on, get!

38
00:02:09,810 --> 00:02:11,730
You're really sure about this?

39
00:02:12,300 --> 00:02:14,690
This thing is not your nephew.

40
00:02:14,690 --> 00:02:17,110
It's just something with
your nephew's information.

41
00:02:17,440 --> 00:02:19,890
You're trying to tell me
I can't live in the present

42
00:02:19,890 --> 00:02:23,260
if I stay hung up on the
dead forever, right?

43
00:02:24,560 --> 00:02:25,940
Still...

44
00:02:25,940 --> 00:02:31,240
My little sister can no longer
live without Takeru.

45
00:02:35,530 --> 00:02:39,580
Masamichi, that lady's
my mother, isn't she?

46
00:02:40,280 --> 00:02:43,470
Yeah. Good job recognizing her.

47
00:02:45,470 --> 00:02:47,350
I had a feeling it was her.

48
00:02:50,160 --> 00:02:51,640
I'm a genius, aren't I?

49
00:02:58,070 --> 00:02:59,190
Takeru!

50
00:03:03,340 --> 00:03:06,000
Takeru!

51
00:03:10,290 --> 00:03:11,650
I'm sorry, but...

52
00:03:12,250 --> 00:03:13,840
I know.

53
00:03:13,840 --> 00:03:17,700
You can't let the existence of your fully
autonomous cursed corpses become known.

54
00:03:18,320 --> 00:03:20,050
So he can't live with her.

55
00:03:20,050 --> 00:03:21,520
I'm sorry.

56
00:03:21,520 --> 00:03:23,670
Why are you apologizing?

57
00:03:24,950 --> 00:03:26,730
Thanks a lot.

58
00:03:27,770 --> 00:03:28,920
I mean it.

59
00:03:29,880 --> 00:03:30,970
Thank you.

60
00:03:32,690 --> 00:03:37,110
Where do you think you're going without
any cursed corpses, Principal Yaga?

61
00:03:38,110 --> 00:03:39,900
To see my son.

62
00:03:40,220 --> 00:03:41,940
Since you've been sentenced to death,

63
00:03:41,940 --> 00:03:44,980
allow me to tell you the
one way to save your life.

64
00:03:45,390 --> 00:03:50,370
Disclose how you create those fully
autonomous man-made cursed corpses!

65
00:03:51,420 --> 00:03:55,120
You all sure grew bold the
moment Satoru was gone.

66
00:04:25,690 --> 00:04:26,610
Principal.

67
00:04:27,230 --> 00:04:30,560
I'll handle the rest, so you may leave.

68
00:04:30,560 --> 00:04:31,530
Understood.

69
00:04:32,850 --> 00:04:38,310
You use the body's information to
reproduce the soul's information.

70
00:04:38,310 --> 00:04:42,710
Then you place that soul information
in the cursed corpse's core.

71
00:04:45,890 --> 00:04:48,240
That's not enough, though.

72
00:04:48,240 --> 00:04:51,100
You have to place cores housing
three highly compatible souls

73
00:04:51,100 --> 00:04:53,060
into a single cursed corpse,

74
00:04:53,730 --> 00:04:57,850
and make those souls observe
each other at all times.

75
00:04:58,230 --> 00:04:59,990
Doing that

76
00:04:59,990 --> 00:05:04,200
finally allows the souls to stabilize
so self-awareness can take root.

77
00:05:04,200 --> 00:05:06,830
Roughly three months after that's born,

78
00:05:06,830 --> 00:05:09,520
it will begin supplying
its own cursed energy.

79
00:05:09,520 --> 00:05:10,970
Why?!

80
00:05:12,510 --> 00:05:14,670
Why share that now?!

81
00:05:15,660 --> 00:05:18,250
Why wouldn't you reveal that sooner?!

82
00:05:18,250 --> 00:05:20,740
Why didn't you try to live longer?!

83
00:05:21,450 --> 00:05:23,210
Because...

84
00:05:23,210 --> 00:05:26,490
it's a curse, Principal Gakuganji.

85
00:05:27,000 --> 00:05:31,240
A curse from me to you.

86
00:05:34,950 --> 00:05:36,110
Masamichi!

87
00:05:46,540 --> 00:05:48,610
Why don't you fight?

88
00:05:48,610 --> 00:05:50,530
Do you not hate me?

89
00:05:51,410 --> 00:05:54,050
Pandas aren't bound by things like that.

90
00:05:54,800 --> 00:05:58,150
Besides, you were never on
bad terms with Masamichi.

91
00:05:59,000 --> 00:06:03,050
To me, you're just the
knife that fell upon him.

92
00:06:04,760 --> 00:06:08,050
Just make sure you remember this...

93
00:06:08,470 --> 00:06:12,050
Even pandas cry.

94
00:06:30,450 --> 00:06:31,160
JUJUTSU KAISEN

95
00:06:54,430 --> 00:06:58,640
JUJUTSU KAISEN
The Culling Game Part 1

96
00:07:50,390 --> 00:07:54,380
Kinji Hakari is currently earning money
as a bookie for a fight club he's running

97
00:07:54,380 --> 00:07:57,490
in an abandoned multi-story
parking garage in Tochigi Prefecture.

98
00:07:57,950 --> 00:07:59,440
A fight club?

99
00:07:59,440 --> 00:08:02,000
They host fist fights between sorcerers.

100
00:08:02,000 --> 00:08:03,930
Then the spectators are...

101
00:08:03,930 --> 00:08:06,250
Generally non-sorcerers.

102
00:08:06,760 --> 00:08:11,190
That blatantly violates the secrecy
mandated in Article 8 of the Jujutsu Code.

103
00:08:09,000 --> 00:08:10,590
ARTICLE 8 - SECRECY: SORCERERS MUST NOT
REVEAL THE EXISTENCE OF SORCERY, CURSES,
AND CURSED OBJECTS TO NON-SORCERERS.
HOWEVER, THIS SHALL NOT APPLY WHEN
IT IS NECESSARY TO FULFILL
THE DUTIES OF THE PREVIOUS ARTICLE.

104
00:08:10,590 --> 00:08:12,970
SECRECY

105
00:08:11,730 --> 00:08:15,140
There are probably curse users among
the participants in the fights, as well.

106
00:08:15,140 --> 00:08:17,040
Do be careful.

107
00:08:20,050 --> 00:08:21,270
Why are we changing?

108
00:08:21,610 --> 00:08:24,750
Hakari-san was expelled for
clashing with the upper brass.

109
00:08:24,750 --> 00:08:27,240
He's also actively violating
jujutsu regulations.

110
00:08:27,650 --> 00:08:30,890
If he finds out we're with
Jujutsu High, he might run.

111
00:08:30,890 --> 00:08:33,160
It's like we're cops and he's the robber.

112
00:08:33,810 --> 00:08:34,900
Hmm?

113
00:08:35,200 --> 00:08:37,370
We're on Jujutsu High's side now?

114
00:08:37,370 --> 00:08:38,890
We're in a gray zone,

115
00:08:38,890 --> 00:08:41,690
but in Hakari-san's eyes,
at least, we're with them.

116
00:08:41,690 --> 00:08:44,170
Is he likely to cooperate
with us in the first place?

117
00:08:44,170 --> 00:08:45,670
I'm not sure.

118
00:08:45,670 --> 00:08:48,350
All our senpai say he's
a good-for-nothing,

119
00:08:49,030 --> 00:08:52,430
but Okkotsu-senpai claimed
he's stronger than him.

120
00:08:53,340 --> 00:08:55,060
We definitely want his strength.

121
00:08:55,650 --> 00:08:57,170
Go home, brats.

122
00:08:57,530 --> 00:08:59,810
This isn't a place for you to hang out.

123
00:08:59,810 --> 00:09:02,470
You have until the count
of three to turn around.

124
00:09:02,470 --> 00:09:05,270
Any other choices will
earn a beating from me.

125
00:09:05,270 --> 00:09:06,640
We need money.

126
00:09:06,640 --> 00:09:09,150
Let us enter the fights held here.

127
00:09:11,880 --> 00:09:13,570
The first rule is:

128
00:09:14,000 --> 00:09:16,830
You do not talk about the fight club.

129
00:09:17,420 --> 00:09:19,720
Now answer me. Who told you?

130
00:09:19,720 --> 00:09:22,040
You'll get your beating after that.

131
00:09:22,040 --> 00:09:23,550
I don't know his name.

132
00:09:23,550 --> 00:09:24,580
I killed him.

133
00:09:25,290 --> 00:09:26,850
It was about a month ago.

134
00:09:27,260 --> 00:09:29,620
He was some scumbag who was all talk.

135
00:09:29,620 --> 00:09:32,370
Kondo disappeared about a month ago.

136
00:09:33,210 --> 00:09:35,140
I'll fill his slot for you.

137
00:09:35,550 --> 00:09:39,110
Or would you rather I lay you
out in front of the bookie?

138
00:09:39,110 --> 00:09:42,900
Oh, yeah. He'd be wary if we
suddenly asked to see him.

139
00:09:42,900 --> 00:09:45,410
I guess we shouldn't know
his name's Hakari, either.

140
00:09:42,900 --> 00:09:43,670
Yes.

141
00:09:44,400 --> 00:09:46,400
No, there's no proof.

142
00:09:45,730 --> 00:09:47,210
Time to zip the lips.

143
00:09:46,860 --> 00:09:47,900
Are you sure?

144
00:09:48,570 --> 00:09:49,970
That's enough.

145
00:09:50,660 --> 00:09:52,650
The boss has given you the go-ahead.

146
00:09:52,650 --> 00:09:55,460
We'll pit you against
today's seeded fighter.

147
00:09:55,460 --> 00:09:56,780
However...

148
00:09:56,780 --> 00:09:58,620
he's the one fighting.

149
00:10:00,800 --> 00:10:02,120
That's good for us.

150
00:10:02,120 --> 00:10:04,360
Itadori's better suited to the fighting.

151
00:10:04,760 --> 00:10:06,830
No go. I'll fight.

152
00:10:06,830 --> 00:10:09,160
Boss said he doesn't like you.

153
00:10:07,160 --> 00:10:09,170
Boss

154
00:10:09,590 --> 00:10:11,740
If you don't like it, the deal's off.

155
00:10:12,940 --> 00:10:15,470
Fine. We'll take it, then.

156
00:10:15,940 --> 00:10:17,920
Fushiguro, that was risky.

157
00:10:17,920 --> 00:10:19,470
Your bluffs went too far.

158
00:10:19,470 --> 00:10:20,920
That's not actually true.

159
00:10:21,380 --> 00:10:25,510
If curse users are participating too,
that means there must be decent turnover.

160
00:10:25,930 --> 00:10:26,930
More importantly...

161
00:10:26,930 --> 00:10:28,750
Yeah, they're here.

162
00:10:29,180 --> 00:10:31,820
If he was watching us
through security cameras,

163
00:10:32,130 --> 00:10:35,110
there's a high chance
Hakari-senpai is in here.

164
00:10:35,110 --> 00:10:37,840
Itadori, you snoop around
from the inside.

165
00:10:37,840 --> 00:10:41,130
I'll snoop around that parking
lot in the meantime.

166
00:10:41,130 --> 00:10:41,810
Maybe.

167
00:10:41,810 --> 00:10:42,880
Maybe?

168
00:10:42,880 --> 00:10:44,860
He's probably leaving me
to my own devices.

169
00:10:44,860 --> 00:10:46,690
If he learns we're infiltrating his club,

170
00:10:46,690 --> 00:10:50,210
we'll lose his trust and our opportunity
to make contact with Hakari-san.

171
00:10:50,570 --> 00:10:53,670
Well, we'll just resort to
force if that happens.

172
00:10:53,960 --> 00:10:56,250
That's really our last resort.

173
00:10:56,250 --> 00:11:01,010
We're only here to ask Hakari-san
for his cooperation.

174
00:11:01,010 --> 00:11:03,890
I'd like to avoid anything that'll
affect our future relations.

175
00:11:04,500 --> 00:11:07,460
To be honest, I don't think I
should be doing anything tonight.

176
00:11:08,040 --> 00:11:10,810
But I don't want to waste the time
we have until Tsumiki is required

177
00:11:10,810 --> 00:11:12,710
to declare her participation
in the Culling Game.

178
00:11:13,430 --> 00:11:14,860
Right now...

179
00:11:14,860 --> 00:11:16,590
it's 5 PM on the 10th.

180
00:11:17,080 --> 00:11:18,990
So nine days until the deadline, huh?

181
00:11:18,990 --> 00:11:22,410
It took longer to get
here than we thought.

182
00:11:22,770 --> 00:11:26,170
That's why I'll be trying to
look for Hakari-san tonight,

183
00:11:26,650 --> 00:11:28,940
but if it looks risky, I'll pull out.

184
00:11:28,940 --> 00:11:30,630
That's why I say "maybe."

185
00:11:30,630 --> 00:11:31,550
Got it.

186
00:11:33,540 --> 00:11:35,390
There are only two rules.

187
00:11:35,390 --> 00:11:38,050
No running away,
and no using cursed techniques.

188
00:11:38,050 --> 00:11:38,980
How come?

189
00:11:38,980 --> 00:11:42,030
I don't mind if they're
using cursed techniques.

190
00:11:42,030 --> 00:11:44,100
Because most of the spectators
are non-sorcerers,

191
00:11:44,100 --> 00:11:45,490
those who can't see them.

192
00:11:45,490 --> 00:11:48,000
A fight people can't see
won't excite them.

193
00:11:48,350 --> 00:11:49,970
And the "no running" rule?

194
00:11:50,250 --> 00:11:53,480
It means you fight where
the spectators can see you.

195
00:11:53,480 --> 00:11:55,850
It's all about the spectators, huh?

196
00:11:55,850 --> 00:11:57,140
Of course.

197
00:11:57,140 --> 00:11:58,350
This is a business.

198
00:11:58,960 --> 00:12:00,430
What's the boss like?

199
00:12:01,790 --> 00:12:02,810
You curious?

200
00:12:03,460 --> 00:12:04,770
Well, yeah.

201
00:12:05,340 --> 00:12:06,910
You'll know if you meet him.

202
00:12:06,910 --> 00:12:07,920
Can I meet him?

203
00:12:09,210 --> 00:12:11,280
There are two kinds of matches.

204
00:12:11,280 --> 00:12:15,170
Real beat-downs, like in today's
tournament, and fixed bouts.

205
00:12:15,660 --> 00:12:17,780
The boss writes the script for those.

206
00:12:18,340 --> 00:12:21,300
He might call for you if you
manage to shine out there.

207
00:12:21,960 --> 00:12:24,920
In other words, I just need
to put on a good show.

208
00:12:24,920 --> 00:12:27,250
That makes things simple.

209
00:12:36,810 --> 00:12:39,970
That's your opponent.

210
00:12:42,590 --> 00:12:45,960
I was blown away the first
time I saw him, too.

211
00:12:45,960 --> 00:12:46,610
Yeah.

212
00:12:47,230 --> 00:12:49,540
It's really all about
drawing in the crowd.

213
00:12:51,900 --> 00:12:54,500
Now, we're getting started again tonight!

214
00:12:54,500 --> 00:12:57,530
It's time for the
Gachinko Fight Club Tournament!

215
00:12:57,530 --> 00:13:01,110
Commentary will be provided by me,
your very own John☆Bobby!

216
00:13:01,110 --> 00:13:04,490
Allow me to introduce tonight's
exciting match-up!

217
00:13:04,490 --> 00:13:06,330
We're joined by a sudden upstart!

218
00:13:06,330 --> 00:13:08,240
Will he rise up or burn out?!

219
00:13:08,240 --> 00:13:13,170
It's the Dangerous Fireball Kid,
Yuji Itadori!

220
00:13:13,170 --> 00:13:18,690
He stands like a panda, sits like
a panda, and walks like a panda!

221
00:13:18,690 --> 00:13:22,630
It's Panda!

222
00:13:21,820 --> 00:13:24,990
Fighting Arena

223
00:13:21,820 --> 00:13:24,990
2nd Floor CH 6

224
00:13:22,630 --> 00:13:24,270
Now, place your bets, place your bets!

225
00:13:24,270 --> 00:13:25,470
Everyone ready?!

226
00:13:25,470 --> 00:13:27,610
Let's get ready to rumble!

227
00:13:27,610 --> 00:13:30,530
I can feel my passion draining away.

228
00:13:30,530 --> 00:13:32,700
What's wrong, Kin-chan?

229
00:13:32,700 --> 00:13:36,560
Luck is meant to be tested, you know.

230
00:13:36,560 --> 00:13:38,920
It's boring to gamble when you
know who'll win from the start.

231
00:13:39,370 --> 00:13:43,580
There aren't many stray sorcerers
who are tough enough to beat Panda.

232
00:13:43,580 --> 00:13:44,930
Whoa!

233
00:13:44,930 --> 00:13:48,680
This is the best bout in my
career as a commentator!

234
00:13:45,320 --> 00:13:47,300
Looks like you might be wrong.

235
00:13:47,300 --> 00:13:48,410
Huh?

236
00:13:48,680 --> 00:13:50,980
Fighting Arena

237
00:13:48,680 --> 00:13:50,980
2nd Floor CH 6

238
00:13:52,990 --> 00:13:55,460
Have you been able to see Hakari-senpai?

239
00:13:55,870 --> 00:13:56,670
No.

240
00:13:57,810 --> 00:13:58,520
Tap

241
00:14:01,830 --> 00:14:04,470
He's not wary of me since
we know each other,

242
00:14:04,470 --> 00:14:06,020
but he's avoiding me.

243
00:14:06,200 --> 00:14:07,280
Tap Tap Tap Tap

244
00:14:07,860 --> 00:14:09,110
Roooar

245
00:14:09,110 --> 00:14:10,450
Roooar

246
00:14:10,710 --> 00:14:14,280
The other third-year's
technique is also a problem.

247
00:14:23,510 --> 00:14:26,250
You're hiding the fact that you're
from Jujutsu High, right?

248
00:14:26,250 --> 00:14:27,330
Yeah.

249
00:14:28,750 --> 00:14:29,990
Good, good.

250
00:14:29,990 --> 00:14:31,470
You know what to do now, right?

251
00:14:37,640 --> 00:14:38,680
Whoa!

252
00:14:38,680 --> 00:14:42,880
This is definitely the best bout
in my career as a commentator!

253
00:14:42,880 --> 00:14:45,980
Though I've only been one for two weeks!

254
00:14:50,860 --> 00:14:51,610
Tap

255
00:14:53,410 --> 00:14:53,710
Tap

256
00:14:55,700 --> 00:14:56,240
Tap

257
00:14:57,330 --> 00:15:00,000
Tap Tap Tap

258
00:15:04,380 --> 00:15:04,880
Tap

259
00:15:11,260 --> 00:15:14,850
The winner: Itadori!

260
00:15:15,480 --> 00:15:17,750
What a punch!

261
00:15:17,750 --> 00:15:18,810
I can't move!

262
00:15:18,810 --> 00:15:22,970
The SPCA won't stand for this!

263
00:15:23,220 --> 00:15:24,600
Your acting sucks.

264
00:15:23,440 --> 00:15:24,600
Your acting sucks.

265
00:15:24,600 --> 00:15:28,260
Send Itadori up to the roof
when the tournament's over.

266
00:15:28,260 --> 00:15:28,890
Huh?

267
00:15:28,890 --> 00:15:30,380
He's sure to win it.

268
00:15:30,380 --> 00:15:33,540
Plus, he's intentionally
fighting in three dimensions

269
00:15:33,540 --> 00:15:35,760
to wow the spectators on the upper floors.

270
00:15:35,760 --> 00:15:37,930
I can write a good script with him.

271
00:15:37,930 --> 00:15:39,080
And like I always say,

272
00:15:40,430 --> 00:15:43,740
strike while the iron's hot.

273
00:15:44,090 --> 00:15:46,450
That's so dumb. Cut it out.

274
00:15:46,450 --> 00:15:49,930
Got it. And what about the other brat?

275
00:15:49,930 --> 00:15:52,300
Continue to be vigilant.

276
00:15:52,300 --> 00:15:54,290
I'll send Kirara for
extra security later.

277
00:15:54,290 --> 00:15:55,340
Huh?

278
00:15:55,340 --> 00:15:57,540
I'm feeling a nice buzz now.

279
00:15:57,540 --> 00:16:03,430
I haven't felt this alive since
my ex maxed out my credit cards.

280
00:16:03,430 --> 00:16:05,780
Quit bringing up your ex.

281
00:16:04,980 --> 00:16:06,940
Jujutsu High Third-Year, Kinji Hakari

282
00:16:04,980 --> 00:16:06,940
Jujutsu High Third-Year,  Kirara Hoshi

283
00:16:08,680 --> 00:16:10,180
I see.

284
00:16:10,180 --> 00:16:13,130
It sounds like Itadori's going
to be able to contact Hakari.

285
00:16:13,520 --> 00:16:17,540
Why haven't you been able to
see him yet, Panda-senpai?

286
00:16:17,540 --> 00:16:20,330
Well, I do know where he is.

287
00:16:20,330 --> 00:16:22,640
In the monitor room on the roof.

288
00:16:22,640 --> 00:16:25,100
But I can't get close.

289
00:16:25,550 --> 00:16:26,970
You can't get close?

290
00:16:26,970 --> 00:16:30,290
Even when I approach the door,
I can't close the distance.

291
00:16:30,290 --> 00:16:33,750
The sensation feels similar
to Satoru's technique.

292
00:16:33,750 --> 00:16:36,750
It's probably due to Kirara's technique.

293
00:16:36,750 --> 00:16:38,190
Kirara?

294
00:16:38,190 --> 00:16:40,870
But the other third-year was a guy, right?

295
00:16:40,870 --> 00:16:42,250
Yeah.

296
00:16:42,250 --> 00:16:46,600
So does that phenomenon only occur
when Kirara-san's in the monitor room?

297
00:16:46,600 --> 00:16:48,050
I don't know.

298
00:16:48,050 --> 00:16:52,830
I focused on being a circus panda instead
of pushing too far and making them run off.

299
00:16:52,830 --> 00:16:55,160
I'm glad you two showed up.

300
00:16:55,610 --> 00:16:58,200
Do you think Itadori will
succeed in persuading him?

301
00:16:58,200 --> 00:17:02,390
It'll be tough,
but I think it's just a matter of time.

302
00:17:02,390 --> 00:17:06,820
Itadori's bright, charming personality
is a good match for Hakari.

303
00:17:06,820 --> 00:17:08,950
But he sucks at lying, doesn't he?

304
00:17:08,950 --> 00:17:10,770
He doesn't just suck at it.

305
00:17:10,770 --> 00:17:13,330
He struggles to even see
lying as an option.

306
00:17:13,330 --> 00:17:17,540
So once Itadori enters
the monitor room,

307
00:17:17,540 --> 00:17:20,070
I'll take control of the
place quickly and quietly

308
00:17:20,070 --> 00:17:23,040
so I can buy time for the
two of them to talk.

309
00:17:23,040 --> 00:17:24,140
No, that's not...

310
00:17:24,140 --> 00:17:25,070
It'll be fine.

311
00:17:25,070 --> 00:17:26,630
I'll just put them to sleep.

312
00:17:26,630 --> 00:17:29,270
I know where the cameras
and their blind spots are.

313
00:17:29,670 --> 00:17:31,100
How many guards are there?

314
00:17:31,360 --> 00:17:32,710
Four at the entrance,

315
00:17:32,710 --> 00:17:35,190
and two on each floor except the roof.

316
00:17:37,740 --> 00:17:39,160
We can handle that.

317
00:17:39,400 --> 00:17:42,540
The only real concern is
Kirara-san's technique.

318
00:17:42,540 --> 00:17:44,580
We can't do anything about that now.

319
00:17:44,580 --> 00:17:48,510
If they can warp Itadori out
of there or warp in backup,

320
00:17:48,510 --> 00:17:51,090
we'll give up on persuading Hakari.

321
00:17:51,090 --> 00:17:53,560
You're still a first-year, Yu-chan?

322
00:17:53,560 --> 00:17:54,870
You're young.

323
00:17:54,870 --> 00:17:55,620
"Yu-chan"?

324
00:17:56,050 --> 00:17:58,370
Kin-chan had to repeat
a year in middle school.

325
00:17:58,780 --> 00:18:01,070
You sound happy.

326
00:18:01,680 --> 00:18:02,710
Well, yeah.

327
00:18:03,170 --> 00:18:06,260
It's been a while since
Kin-chan's gotten heated up.

328
00:18:07,190 --> 00:18:11,270
You see, I love it when
Kin-chan is passionate.

329
00:18:16,340 --> 00:18:17,480
Itadori.

330
00:18:18,000 --> 00:18:19,920
Would you believe me if I said

331
00:18:19,920 --> 00:18:24,660
you can earn a million yen a month by
doing something for just one hour a day?

332
00:18:24,960 --> 00:18:26,020
Huh?

333
00:18:26,020 --> 00:18:26,780
Hmm?

334
00:18:27,230 --> 00:18:29,900
Depends on what that "something" is.

335
00:18:29,900 --> 00:18:32,120
But you'll have to pay me 200,000 yen

336
00:18:32,120 --> 00:18:34,930
to buy the information on
what that "something" is.

337
00:18:34,930 --> 00:18:36,000
Huh?

338
00:18:36,650 --> 00:18:38,250
I don't believe you, then.

339
00:18:38,250 --> 00:18:43,090
Good. Like you suspected,
that's a classic con.

340
00:18:43,090 --> 00:18:47,300
The swindler pretends to be rich
and sells the means to becoming rich

341
00:18:47,300 --> 00:18:49,060
to scam money from others.

342
00:18:49,060 --> 00:18:51,390
It's obvious if you
think about it logically,

343
00:18:51,390 --> 00:18:54,230
but there's a stupid amount
of fools who fall for it.

344
00:18:54,230 --> 00:18:55,600
Why?

345
00:18:55,600 --> 00:18:58,000
It's all because of passion.

346
00:18:58,000 --> 00:18:59,120
Passion?

347
00:18:59,120 --> 00:19:03,660
Both the swindler and the deceived
have the same passionate drive

348
00:19:03,660 --> 00:19:05,900
to change their lives.

349
00:19:06,770 --> 00:19:10,020
People high on passion lose
sight of their judgment.

350
00:19:10,020 --> 00:19:13,540
Yet no one can fall in love
without passion, either.

351
00:19:14,030 --> 00:19:16,520
I love that passion.

352
00:19:17,080 --> 00:19:21,200
Do you know the most direct way
for people to deal with passion?

353
00:19:22,010 --> 00:19:23,090
Gambling?

354
00:19:26,130 --> 00:19:28,920
I knew you would get it.

355
00:19:29,510 --> 00:19:31,550
Life is a gamble.

356
00:19:32,000 --> 00:19:35,660
Loads of women have dumped me
because they hate gambling,

357
00:19:35,660 --> 00:19:38,080
but they've got it wrong.

358
00:19:38,780 --> 00:19:41,710
Our society throws out
those who can't bet big

359
00:19:41,710 --> 00:19:45,020
and those who don't know when to fold.

360
00:19:45,320 --> 00:19:48,570
There isn't a single person
who doesn't gamble.

361
00:19:48,570 --> 00:19:51,730
What people hate isn't the gambling,

362
00:19:51,730 --> 00:19:54,040
it's losing and being ruined.

363
00:19:54,400 --> 00:19:57,420
Aren't there people who just want
to live a peaceful life, too?

364
00:19:57,420 --> 00:19:59,850
I don't know anyone like that.

365
00:20:00,580 --> 00:20:03,180
I love passion.

366
00:20:03,590 --> 00:20:07,580
Passion is gambling,
and gambling is life.

367
00:20:07,580 --> 00:20:10,000
And love is control.

368
00:20:10,510 --> 00:20:15,150
In the future, I want to control this
nation's passion through my fight club.

369
00:20:15,650 --> 00:20:19,650
With the existence of curses going public
and headquarters barely able to function,

370
00:20:19,650 --> 00:20:22,240
this is my chance to expand the business.

371
00:20:22,760 --> 00:20:24,990
I'm going to crush the
obstacles before me

372
00:20:24,990 --> 00:20:28,620
and make them publicly recognize
my fight club in the coming revisions

373
00:20:28,620 --> 00:20:30,370
to the jujutsu regulations.

374
00:20:31,010 --> 00:20:35,140
At any rate, I'll need a
strong piece on the board.

375
00:20:36,280 --> 00:20:37,620
Itadori...

376
00:20:38,490 --> 00:20:41,650
Want to get high on my passion?

377
00:20:42,740 --> 00:20:45,060
Boss, I need to—

378
00:20:57,620 --> 00:21:00,050
Itadori, want something to drink?

379
00:21:00,050 --> 00:21:02,060
Oh, I'm good with anything.

380
00:21:02,060 --> 00:21:03,420
Other than liquor.

381
00:21:03,420 --> 00:21:05,460
What, can't handle it?

382
00:21:05,800 --> 00:21:08,120
That's not the issue. I'm still underage.

383
00:21:08,120 --> 00:21:10,620
You don't strike me as the
type to care about that.

384
00:21:10,620 --> 00:21:13,760
Did you know Satoru Gojo
can't hold his liquor, either?

385
00:21:13,760 --> 00:21:16,270
Really? Who's Gojo?

386
00:21:16,270 --> 00:21:18,980
And I never said I couldn't.

387
00:21:18,980 --> 00:21:20,310
Look.

388
00:21:20,310 --> 00:21:21,060
Huh?

389
00:21:28,780 --> 00:21:32,450
There isn't a single sorcerer who
doesn't know of Satoru Gojo.

390
00:21:32,450 --> 00:21:34,270
So why did you feign ignorance?

391
00:21:34,270 --> 00:21:35,510
Were you...

392
00:21:42,050 --> 00:21:43,800
sent by Jujutsu High?

393
00:21:50,930 --> 00:21:52,380
Listen! I—

394
00:21:52,850 --> 00:21:54,260
H-Hey!

395
00:21:54,260 --> 00:21:55,650
L-Lis—

396
00:21:55,650 --> 00:21:58,400
When I get a call from Kirara's number,

397
00:21:58,400 --> 00:22:00,850
it's a signal something's up.

398
00:22:03,100 --> 00:22:04,130
Listen to me!

399
00:22:04,130 --> 00:22:05,290
Hell no!

400
00:22:05,290 --> 00:22:06,970
My passion's gone cold now!

401
00:22:06,970 --> 00:22:09,970
Episode 52
Passion

402
00:23:40,420 --> 00:23:42,230
If we can convince them,

403
00:23:42,230 --> 00:23:44,390
negotiations with Hakari-san
will go more smoothly!

404
00:23:43,740 --> 00:23:45,260
Wait, Kirara!

405
00:23:45,260 --> 00:23:46,240
Stay out of this!

406
00:23:46,240 --> 00:23:49,090
You have to show me!
Right here and now!

407
00:23:49,090 --> 00:23:51,020
Please! There's no time!

408
00:23:51,020 --> 00:23:53,460
Kin-chan's in danger!

409
00:23:51,990 --> 00:23:55,060
Next Episode
Cog
